atus, or state explicitly that no findings block is attached when status is `unknown`.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gate_run_status returns status 'unknown' when read_gate_run is None and _inflight.is_job_active is False (gate_runs.py:158-160), so 'unknown' is a live status a poller can see.","The Disposition enumerates run-running, run-attaching, run-stale-running but never run-unknown; the non-terminal AC says only `reason=\"run-<status>\"` which would synthesize an undocumented `run-unknown` value not listed in the vocabulary.","ABSENCE: no plan text states whether an `unknown`-status job carries a findings block at all or what readable/reason it reports."],"finding":"The findings.reason enum omits a value for the `unknown` gate-run status (no index record and not in-flight), so an executor computing the findings block for that status has no defined reason and no stated readable value.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f78ed438d1f650f2f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 6-7 / Disposition paragraph; ACs for non-terminal runs (`reason=\"run-<status>\"`)","norm_id":"n600f81c1e2683d06","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caller polls a job_id whose index entry was pruned/lost and whose daemon already exited; gate_status returns status 'unknown' and the executor must emit a findings.reason the plan never defined."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add `run-unknown` to the reason vocabulary (readable=false, reviewed_at=null) or document that `unknown` jobs return no findings block, mirroring the run-<status> mapping.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that pins `findings.latest_reviewed_at` semantics (e.g. it reflects the newest-by-ticket sidecar timestamp and is never used to infer readability), or drop the field if it is purely informational.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Item 6: 'gate_status(job_id) adds findings for plan-review jobs: sidecar_type, readable, reason, reviewed_at, latest_reviewed_at, and legacy diagnostic job_started_at.'","No AC line references latest_reviewed_at; ACs assert reviewed_at=null for non-terminal, reason strings, sidecar_type, readable — but never latest_reviewed_at."],"finding":"The `findings.latest_reviewed_at` field introduced in Fix plan item 6 has no covering acceptance criterion; every other findings field (sidecar_type, readable, reason, reviewed_at, job_started_at) is asserted by at least one AC, but nothing verifies latest_reviewed_at's value or provenance.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f909ed085212313cf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan item 6 / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nafc3a6d17a2adc48","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer could populate latest_reviewed_at incorrectly (or omit it) and every AC would still pass."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'Seed a newer same-ticket sidecar than the job's receipt and assert findings.latest_reviewed_at reflects the newest-by-ticket timestamp while findings.readable stays gated on the exact receipt.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the findings.reason (and readable=false) for a terminal `failed` run that recorded no sidecar_reviewed_at receipt.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_spawn_gate_daemon sets status='failed' and verdict=str(error) in the except branch (_mcp_llm.py:162-167,169-179) — no review result exists, so steps 5's copy of sidecar_emitted/sidecar_reviewed_at from the completed review result has nothing to copy.","Disposition defines terminal-unavailable reasons only for sidecar-not-emitted and review-result-generation-unknown (legacy), and readable paths; it never states which reason a `failed` terminal (no receipt, non-legacy) reports.","ABSENCE: no plan text or AC covers the terminal `failed` status readability disposition."],"finding":"The plan does not map a `failed` terminal run (the gate raised before producing a verdict, so no sidecar_reviewed_at receipt is recorded) to a findings.reason, leaving the fallback for a failed sub-step unspecified for that terminal path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f447b7c006052d2f5","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan steps 5-7 / Disposition; AC on terminal sidecar_emitted=false paths","norm_id":"nf3a3cb9e60ec31e8","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The plan-review daemon throws (provider outage/exception) before emitting a verdict; the run index records status='failed' with no receipt, and gate_status must still emit a findings block for a plan-review job."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that a terminal `failed` run with no receipt reports readable=false with reason `sidecar-not-emitted` (or a dedicated `run-failed`), and add a covering AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the reuse-path sidecar_reviewed_at is the ns-timestamp of the exact file whose payload latest_review_result() actually returned (not the newest filename prefix from latest_review_timestamp), so the receipt and the readable exact-prefix file are the same file when a newer corrupt/unsupported sidecar exists.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 4: reuse paths 'set sidecar_reviewed_at from the reused sidecar's filename timestamp'","sidecar.latest_review_result walks newest→oldest and 'returns the first usable plan_review_result_v1/_v2 payload (a malformed newest file is logged, once)' — the reused file is not necessarily the newest","sidecar.latest_review_timestamp returns files[-1] prefix (newest) 'without a JSON parse' — no usability check","AC: 'terminal sidecar_emitted=false with a reused sidecar_reviewed_at reports findings.readable=true for that exact sidecar'","gate_status readable=true only when the EXACT-prefix file 'parses as a supported plan_review_result_v1/v2 payload' (step 7)"],"finding":"The reuse short-circuit receipt (step 4) may point at the newest REVIEW_RESULT filename rather than the file whose payload was actually reused, because latest_review_result() walks back over corrupt/unsupported newest files to an older usable payload while the only filename-timestamp helper (latest_review_timestamp) returns the newest prefix unconditionally.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa3fe8b64ec0a3778","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan step 4; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py (idempotent_reuse/verdict_reuse, _replay_anchor); src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py:184-197 vs 264-295","norm_id":"n57419977303dabd6","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket whose newest REVIEW_RESULT file is a mid-emit-crash corrupt file, with an older valid BLOCK/PASS payload that verdict_reuse/idempotent_reuse replays","A schema-bumped (unsupported) newest sidecar with an older supported one"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have latest_review_result (or a sibling reader) return the reused file's ns-prefix alongside the payload, and set sidecar_reviewed_at from that value in idempotent_reuse/verdict_reuse; do not derive the reuse receipt from latest_review_timestamp, which ignores usability.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522